---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { galleryImage, portfolioPairs, portfolioRepairs } from '../../data/gallery';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Paintless Dent Repair Before & After Gallery | Peak Country';
const description = 'View real Paintless Dent Repair before-and-after examples, organized by vehicle with paired and additional context views.';
const canonical = new URL('/gallery/', site.url).href;
const photos = portfolioRepairs.flatMap((repair) => repair.photos.map((photo) => ({ repair, photo })));
const imageNodes = photos.map(({repair,photo}) => ({
  '@type':'ImageObject',
  '@id':`${canonical}#${repair.slug}-${photo.state}-${photo.angle}`,
  contentUrl:new URL(galleryImage(repair,photo,1200,'jpg'),site.url).href,
  thumbnailUrl:new URL(galleryImage(repair,photo,720,'webp'),site.url).href,
  name:`${repair.vehicle} ${photo.state} paintless dent repair angle ${photo.angle}`,
  caption:photo.caption,
  description:photo.alt,
  width:photo.width,
  height:photo.height,
  about:{'@id':`${site.url}/paintless-dent-repair/#service`},
  isPartOf:{'@id':`${canonical}#webpage`},
}));
const pageSchema = {'@context':'https://schema.org','@graph':[
  {'@type':'ItemList','@id':`${canonical}#portfolio`,name:'Peak Country Paintless Dent Repair portfolio',numberOfItems:imageNodes.length,mainEntityOfPage:{'@id':`${canonical}#webpage`},itemListElement:imageNodes.map((image,index)=>({'@type':'ListItem',position:index+1,item:{'@id':image['@id']}}))},
  ...imageNodes,
]};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} exactTitle pageSchema={pageSchema}>
  <header class="page-head gallery-head"><div class="eyebrow">Real Repair Results</div><h1>Paintless Dent Repair Before &amp; After Gallery</h1><p>Each vehicle is kept together as one repair set, with comparable before-and-after views and any useful additional context shown clearly.</p></header>

  <section class="section gallery-intro">
    <div><div class="eyebrow">Repair proof, organized clearly</div><h2>See the same repair from more than one angle.</h2></div>
    <div><p>Different lighting and viewing angles can reveal different parts of a dent. The photographs below preserve those views and place paired before-and-after angles next to each other where both are available. An unmatched image remains visible as additional context rather than being discarded or presented as a pair.</p><p><em>Portfolio includes current Peak Country repairs and selected work personally completed by the owner throughout his professional PDR career.</em></p></div>
  </section>

  <nav class="section gallery-jump" aria-label="Repair portfolio"><span>View a repair:</span>{portfolioRepairs.map(repair=><a href={`#${repair.slug}`}>{repair.vehicle}</a>)}</nav>

  <div class="portfolio-list">
    {portfolioRepairs.map((repair,index) => <article class="section portfolio-case" id={repair.slug}>
      <header class="portfolio-case-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Repair set · {repair.photos.length} photographs</div><h2>{repair.title}</h2></div><p>{repair.summary}</p></header>
      <div class="portfolio-pairs">
        {portfolioPairs(repair).map((pair) => <section class="portfolio-pair" aria-label={`${repair.vehicle} repair view ${pair.angle}`}>
          <h3>Repair view {pair.angle}{pair.after ? ' · before and after' : ' · additional before context'}</h3>
          <div class="portfolio-grid">
            {[pair.before, pair.after].filter(Boolean).map((photo) => photo && <figure class:list={['portfolio-photo',`portfolio-photo--${photo.state}`]}>
              <a href={galleryImage(repair,photo,1200,'jpg')} aria-label={`View larger image: ${photo.alt}`}>
                <picture>
                  <source type="image/avif" srcset={`${galleryImage(repair,photo,720,'avif')} 720w, ${galleryImage(repair,photo,1200,'avif')} 1200w`} sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 48px), 560px" />
                  <source type="image/webp" srcset={`${galleryImage(repair,photo,720,'webp')} 720w, ${galleryImage(repair,photo,1200,'webp')} 1200w`} sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 48px), 560px" />
                  <img src={galleryImage(repair,photo,1200,'jpg')} width={photo.width} height={photo.height} alt={photo.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
                </picture>
              </a>
              <figcaption><span>{photo.state === 'before' ? 'Before' : 'After'}</span>{photo.caption.replace(/^(Before|After) · Angle \d — /,'')}</figcaption>
            </figure>)}
          </div>
        </section>)}
      </div>
      {index < portfolioRepairs.length - 1 && <a class="portfolio-back" href="#main">Back to gallery introduction ↑</a>}
    </article>)}
  </div>

  <section class="section gallery-explain"><div><div class="eyebrow">What these examples show</div><h2>PDR results begin with the vehicle in front of the technician.</h2></div><div><p>These images demonstrate real dent repairs, but they do not establish that another dent will respond the same way. Paint condition, dent depth, panel location, metal stretch, body lines, and tool access all affect repairability.</p><p>Customer privacy is protected in public repair photography. Plates and unnecessary identifying information are removed, blurred, or avoided when appropriate. Images may be cropped, straightened, or normally adjusted for presentation, but are not altered to remove remaining damage, change panel shape, or create a result that was not achieved.</p><p>Learn <a href="/auto-hail-repair/">how automotive hail damage is evaluated</a>, review the <a href="/paintless-dent-repair/">Paintless Dent Repair process</a>, or <a href="/get-started/">Get Started</a> for your vehicle.</p></div></section>
</Layout>
